  "body": "Fork synced at v0.18.0.\n\n## What changed\n\nReach law (c3), the mid-turn sweep, read the band stack's column at 4 path stations x 5 turn fractions. Between them a holder or shank could cross uncut stock with no `SweepHit` (#1313).\n\nIt now reads the whole reachable set, by construction:\n\n- New module `crates/sim/src/verify/turn_cells.rs`. Per band, one *cell* per tip chord and per interval of the turn. A cell is the convex hull of law (c)'s column at the interval's two end poses, grown by a proven sag, with its bottom at the lower end bottom less the sag.\n- The sag bound: the letters lerp and bend the axis no faster than their own sweep, so inside a cell the axis strays from the chord of its end axes by at most `(sweep in the cell)^2 / 8`; times the band's reach above the tip. The cell count keeps it at 0.001 mm or less, capped at 64 cells per band (a 90 degree turn at 150 mm reach then overstates by 0.011 mm, still conservative).\n- The tip's travel is not sampled either: the hull is clipped against the tip chord exactly, the bottom rides the chord's Z, and the flutes' kerf excuses a column only for the tip positions that stand over it.\n- `sweep.rs` asks a cell one question (`bottom_over`); the column memo and the worst-offender rule are unchanged. `midpose::pose` became `pub(super)` to share the letter lerp.\n\nA refusal is the safe side here: the new reading is a superset of the old one at every pose and station the old grid read.\n\n## How tested\n\n- `crates/sim/tests/midturn_swept_band.rs` - `a_holder_crossing_a_stock_post_between_two_sampled_poses_is_convicted`: a holder 100 mm up the stack swings through a stock post between the 20 and 40 degree samples of an 80 degree turn. Run against main's `sweep.rs` it reports nothing; here it reports `SweepHit { at: 0 }`. Its twin `a_turn_that_stops_short_of_the_post_stays_clean` keeps a clear swing clean.\n- `verify::turn_cells::tests::no_band_position_of_a_random_turn_lies_outside_the_cells` - the issue's brute-force probe: 240 random turns (A and B up to +-85 degrees, a third also in C), 5,076,000 band positions (the true cylinder's surface and law (c)'s own column, 9 path stations x 25 turn fractions). Zero outside the cells, in XY and in Z. The old grid misses 272,961 of the same positions.\n- Three more unit tests: the sag bound at a wall, the kerf following the tip, degenerate bands and non-finite letters.\n- Quick gate `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: sim, motion and app suites green (48 gate-mapped suites, every existing mid-turn test, no assertion edited). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The release lanes (`--ignored`, the big posed fixtures) were not run, so false convictions on real 5-axis programs are not measured. In the debug suites there are none.\n- Verify time on a large posed program was not measured. A small turn needs fewer cells than the old 20 states per band; a large one up to 64.\n- The overhang backstop (stock hidden under a ledge) still asks the old 4 x 5 grid: filed as #1316.\n\nDecision note: `docs/decisions/1313-midturn-swept-band.md`.\n\nChangelog: Verify's mid-turn sweep (law c3) reads every pose and tip position of a turn instead of five sampled poses, so a holder or shank crossing stock between samples is reported\nEffort: max (not escalated)\n\nFixes #1313\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
